 411:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   * @note   The HSI is used (enabled by hardware) as system clock source after
 412:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         startup from Reset, wake-up from STOP and STANDBY mode, or in case
 413:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         of failure of the HSE used directly or indirectly as system clock
 414:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         (if the Clock Security System CSS is enabled).
 415:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *
 416:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   * @note   A switch from one clock source to another occurs only if the target
 417:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         clock source is ready (clock stable after startup delay or PLL locked).
 418:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         If a clock source which is not yet ready is selected, the switch will
 419:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *         occur when the clock source will be ready.
 420:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   *
 421:../.././hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/stm32f4/stm32f4_hal_lowlevel.c ****   * @note   Depending on the device voltage range, the software has to set correctly
